A||||5||JohnnyK||Quick questions about dropping the cradle||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||09-26-2000||01:57 PM||||I have about two more bolts to go before the cradle drops, and it is suspended by the two engine lift points on top of the iron duke (Big O's that you attach the engine lift to.) I have the car up on stands, but when I undo the last bolts, I want to know if these hook things will hold the entire engine, cradle, tranny, etc.. thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||cscougar||09-26-2000||02:01 PM||||I have dropped 2 cradles and installed 2 engines so far and in 2 weeks will do another.  As long as you have the engine lifted by the 2 hooks on the block, then that supports all the engine, transmission and cradle.  Just have all the lines and wires loose and lower the cradle and engine down to the ground.  You might have to raise the body up to get the cradle and all out from under it later.||||reg||1
Z||000002||cscougar||09-26-2000||02:02 PM||||I have dropped 2 cradles and installed 2 engines so far and in 2 weeks will do another.  As long as you have the engine lifted by the 2 hooks on the block, then that supports all the engine, transmission and cradle.  Just have all the lines and wires loose and lower the cradle and engine down to the ground.  You might have to raise the body up to get the cradle and all out from under it later.||||reg||1
Z||000003||JohnnyK||09-26-2000||02:52 PM||||Yeah.. All thats ready, I just wanted to know if those hooks would support everything! Thanks man||||reg||1
Z||000004||JohnnyK||09-26-2000||04:30 PM||||Also, how level will those two hooks hold it? If I undo the back bolts, and then the front, will it suddenly swing down and crush my arm?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||cscougar||09-26-2000||06:02 PM||||I take the front nuts off but not the bolts, then the back bolts and finally the front bolts.  Just make sure the cradle is snug up to the frame with the chain lift and it should not swing or anything.  After its loose you can lower the entire cradle.  It really is an easy job, just make sure all the wires and hoses are disconnected.<BR>||||reg||1
